Z||000000||kslish||07-25-2001||12:01 AM||||I've been working occasionally on my '88 Formula trying to get it running right.  It's been a pain in the rear since I got it....the engine was rebuilt less than 1000 miles ago by the previous owner but I've been chasing various wiring gremlins since I got it trying to get it running right.<P>Since I've had it, I've replaced the O2 sensor, the temp guage sender (to get the dash guage to read anything besides cold), and the fan switch.  The cold start injector wasn't even plugged in and various other connectors were cracked that I have fixed.  Even though the internals of the engine are new, it looks like everything bolted to the engine is pretty much original.<P>Recently it started running terrible again, idling high, stumbling and/or stalling when warm.  Checking the codes resulted in a Code 15.  Should I start by replacing the ECM coolent sensor, or is there something I should look at and/or troubleshoot first?  <P>The reason I'm thinking it's definately the sensor is because the rest of the coolant related sensors have gone bad (fan switch, guage sender) and have needed replacement but I thought I'd poll the board first before dropping the $$.<P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-25-2001||06:42 AM||||High idle and code 15, is more than likely the temp sensor.||||reg||1
